│ │            it from this repo). Cyrillic in briefs/docstrings is intentional, hence `RUF001`–`RUF003` are ignored.\n\n## How a run works (non-obvious invariants)\n\n-  │ │
│ │            **One scenario = one subprocess** (`bench/run_one.py`): `drcode.config` binds `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` at import time, and drcode\'s repo `.env` leaks through     │ │
│ │            pydantic-settings — only a fresh process with a scrubbed env gives clean layered config. The env is sanitized *in place, before* drcode is imported.\n-     │ │
│ │            **Never set `DRCODE_MODEL` / `DRCODE_BASE_URL`**: they override the per-role (coding/tester/compaction) model choice for *all* roles. Role selection comes  │ │
│ │            only from `matrix.toml` → generated `models.json` / `.drcode/drcode.json` files.\n- The harness runs the **real `DrCodeApp` headless** (textual             │ │
│ │            `run_test()`) — never reimplement or fork the drcode pipeline in bench code.\n- The recording wrapper monkeypatches `drcode.agent_model.build_model`        │ │
│ │            *before* app creation; `viewed_id` is never touched (opening a task renders the whole transcript and pollutes timing measurements).\n- `bench run` exit     │ │
│ │            codes: 0 = every job got a verdict (a substantive failure is a data point, not an error), 1 = unresolved infrastructure failures, 2 = planning errors.\n-   │ │
│ │            Artifacts per run land in `runs/<run_id>/` (gitignored): `result.json`, `metrics.json`, `model_log.jsonl`, `user_sim.jsonl`, a `.drcode/` snapshot.         │ │
│ │            `runs/runner-summary.json` holds scheduler history.\n\n## Matrix & scenarios\n\n- `matrix.toml`: providers + `[[combo]]` with exactly three roles           │ │
│ │            (`coding`/`tester`/`compaction`). `api_key` supports `"env:NAME"` substitution. Combo keys like `coding_max_context_tokens = 3000` become per-model catalog │ │
│ │            overrides (used to force compaction without env vars). A model entry may set `model = "<wire-name>"` — the table key becomes a local alias for a real       │ │
│ │            provider model (one provider model, several context caps); alias entries are materialized into virtual providers `<provider>--<alias>` at run prep, and     │ │
│ │            generated configs carry only real wire names.\n- Scenario = `scenarios/<id>/` with `seed/` (copied into the run workspace), `scenario.toml` (briefs,        │ │
│ │            followups, clarification_answers, timeout, `[settle]`), and `checks.py` (harness calls `python checks.py <workspace>`; exit 0 = green). Verdicts are always │ │
│ │            **mechanical** — the harness runs pytest in the workspace itself; never judge by agent words.\n- Task kinds in briefs: `feature`/`bug` only — `research`    │ │
│ │            tasks never reach the tester.\n- Implemented scenarios: S1, S2a, S2b, S3, S4, S5, S6, S7.\n- S7 routes the run through `bench/proxy.py` (§9): a scenario    │ │
│ │            `[proxy]` section enables it with a deterministic fault script (`[[proxy.faults]]`: `http_429`/`drop`/`delay` fired by request counter); `bench run         │ │
│ │            --use-proxy` / `run_one --use-proxy` forces a fault-free recording proxy for any scenario. Proxy log → `runs/<run_id>/proxy_log.jsonl`, aggregated into     │ │
│ │            `metrics.json["proxy"]` (+ `latency_cross_check` against the recorder when both are on). Note: the openai SDK inside drcode retries 429s itself             │ │
│ │            (max_retries=2) — a drcode-visible 429 needs three consecutive 429 faults; connection drops are never SDK-retried.\n- Scenario briefs and docs are written  │ │
│ │            in Russian; code and comments in English — keep that split.\n\n## Testing quirks\n\n- `tests/test_scenarios_e2e.py` drives the **real pipeline end-to-end** │ │
│ │            through `tests/fake_gateway.py` (localhost HTTP/SSE, scripted per model id) — much slower than the unit tests, but no external network. The fake gateway    │ │
│ │            inflates reported usage to genuinely trip drcode\'s compaction gates.\n- In-process runs must monkeypatch                                                   │ │
│ │            `drcode.config._USER_CONFIG_DIR`/`USER_CONFIG_FILE` (config dir is bound at import time) and restore `os.environ` around the test — see `env_guard` and     │ │
│ │            `test_scenarios_e2e.py` for the established pattern.\n- The user simulator (`bench/user_sim.py`) is part of correctness, not a test helper: every           │ │
│ │            intervention goes to `user_sim.jsonl`, and its scenario failures are hard settle-blockers.', run_id='01a167c3-4a44-76a5-ad92-407cf3df5d4e',                 │ │
